---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { href } from '../../lib/site'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Maintenance of the TDED — the original text · UN/TDED"
  description="Section 2 of UNTDED 2005: the TDED Maintenance Agency, its composition and the procedures for changing the directory."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-un-deep">The document · PDF pp. 14–18</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">2 — Maintenance of the TDED</h1>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">The Maintenance Agency</h2>
      <div class="prose-def mt-3 space-y-4">
        <p>
          The Directory is maintained by the TDED Maintenance Agency (MA),
          operating within the United Nations framework for trade
          facilitation — the former UN/ECE Working Party on Facilitation of
          Trade Procedures, now UN/CEFACT, its Forum and empowered groups. It
          is composed of inter-governmental and non-governmental bodies and of
          representatives of ISO national Member Bodies, of ISO TCs (Technical
          Committees) and ISO/IEC JTC1 SCs (Sub-Committees) concerned, each
          being entitled to appoint one official representative.
        </p>
        <p>
          The MA is authorized to seek external expert advice where necessary,
          and may consult directly users of the TDED, national facilitation
          bodies and other interested parties, as required.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Changing the directory</h2>
      <div class="prose-def mt-3 space-y-4">
        <p>
          If it is proposed to change the name or description of a data element
          in such a way that, without substantially changing the concept, its
          application area is extended or further clarified, the numeric
          identifier may be retained provided that there are no objections from
          users who might be adversely affected by the change.
        </p>
        <p>
          If an urgent need arises for the introduction of a new data element,
          or for a change of an existing one, the Maintenance Agency may act
          through its procedures for such cases — the 2005 edition’s change
          indicators record the outcome of exactly this process against the
          1993 edition.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-body">
        See the{' '}
        <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={href('/notation/#change-tags')}>change-tag legend</a>{' '}
        for how each change is marked in the entries.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-10 rounded-md border border-line bg-mist p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-body">
      Transcribed (abridged to the sections reproduced above) from OCR of PDF
      pp. 14–18 (see the{' '}
      <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={href('/document')}>provenance note</a>).
      This maintenance function is what ISO/TC 154 resolution P-2026-07 now
      proposes to run on an open-source platform —{' '}
      <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={href('/about')}>this one</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>